      "notes_markdown": "# CF M01 C12: Shareholder Wealth Maximisation vs Profit Maximisation\n\n## 1. Executive Theoretical Foundation\n\nThe lecture initiates a critical examination of the fundamental objective function in corporate finance: Is Shareholder Wealth Maximisation (SWM) strictly identical to Profit Maximisation (PM)? The unequivocal answer is **no**. The distinction hinges on the temporal dimension of the variables being maximized—specifically, the difference between **Stock Variables** and **Flow Variables**.\n\n### 1.1 Stock Variables vs. Flow Variables\n\nThis conceptual dichotomy is foundational to understanding the objective of the firm.\n\n*   **Stock Variables:** These are variables measured at a **particular point in time**. They represent a snapshot of the entity's condition at a specific moment.\n    *   **Examples:** Wealth, Assets, Liabilities, Equity.\n    *   **Context:** In financial accounting, the Balance Sheet is the primary statement of stock variables. When we read \"Balance Sheet as of 31st March 2026,",
